ata: Relationships (3178, 3181, 3183, 14024, 14025, 14033)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Therapeutic monitoring of 血浆环孢霉素浓度 is critical for safety\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Given its narrow therapeutic index, maintaining 环孢霉素 within target concentration ranges is essential to balance immunosuppression and toxicity. Post-transplant guidelines recommend specific trough levels: 11–15 μg/L in month 1, 8–11 μg/L in months 2–3, and 5–8 μg/L thereafter. Deviations above this range drastically increase 肾中毒 risk. Monitoring 血浆环孢霉素浓度 is further complicated by interacting drugs that unpredictably alter its pharmacokinetics, necessitating frequent assay-based dose adjustments to avoid adverse outcomes [Data: Relationships (3177, 8597, 14032)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Non-renal adverse effects include 雷诺症状 and 面部改观\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond nephrotoxicity, 环孢霉素 is associated with systemic adverse reactions such as 雷诺症状 (Raynaud's phenomenon) and 面部改观 (facial changes). While less common than renal effects, these manifestations indicate broader vascular and connective tissue impacts. The occurrence of 雷诺症状 suggests microvascular dysfunction, possibly linked to the same vasoconstrictive mechanisms affecting renal vasculature. These effects contribute to the drug’s overall burden of toxicity and may affect patient quality of life and treatment adherence [Data: Relationships (14034, 14035)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Drug interactions extend to agents with independent nephrotoxic potential\",\n            \"explanation\": \"环孢霉素 interacts with other nephrotoxic drugs like 苯丙酸氮芥, creating additive or synergistic renal injury risks. Co-administration with such agents is explicitly cautioned against due to dual pathways of kidney damage—direct tubular toxicity from the co-drug and hemodynamic-mediated injury from 环孢霉素. This interaction profile necessitates careful review of concomitant medications in clinical settings to avoid preventable acute kidney injury [Data: Relationships (44122)].\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to 环孢霉素’s narrow therapeutic window, extensive drug interaction profile, and strong association with severe, potentially irreversible renal toxicity.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782126846, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1573, "prompt_tokens": 6894, "total_tokens": 8467, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"环孢霉素-Centric Drug Interaction and Adverse Reaction Network\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on 环孢霉素 (Cyclosporine), a high-degree drug entity with extensive relationships to other drugs, clinical indicators, and adverse effects. 环孢霉素 interacts with multiple medications—including 秋水仙素, KET, 孕激素类, 甲基泼尼松, 甲基睾丸酮, and 苯丙酸氮芥—that can alter its blood concentration or amplify its toxicity. It is strongly associated with renal toxicity (肾中毒), elevated renal vascular resistance, reduced potassium excretion, and hormonal imbalances affecting the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system. Clinical indicators such as 血浆环孢霉素浓度, 血清肌酐清除率, and 肝功 are directly affected by 环孢霉素 use, highlighting its narrow therapeutic window and significant safety implications.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"环孢霉素 is the central hub of a high-risk pharmacological network\",\n            \"explanation\": \"环孢霉素 exhibits the highest degree (100) among all entities, indicating its centrality in this community. It